Volunteers who spend 100+ hours per year volunteering have 27% lower mortality rates than non-volunteers, according to a 2013 study in Psychological Bulletin — a health benefit comparable to regular moderate exercise.
Volunteering in a professional capacity (pro bono legal work, medical volunteering, software development for NGOs) develops skills and networks that advance careers — LinkedIn reports volunteering experience correlates with faster promotion.
Young people who volunteer during education have higher civic engagement, higher graduate employment rates, and higher life satisfaction into adulthood — effects that persist across the 40-year longitudinal Terman study.
